# A lens must not steal the primary's camera, or its own.
#
# The trap this guards (fixed 2026-07-26): `Viewport` carries the camera
# WITHOUT the view size, and `Canvas::resize` re-centres by shifting
# camera.offset half the size delta. So installing a lens camera and THEN
# resizing to the lens rect shifts that camera by the delta between two
# windows' rects; read back and stored, it drifted every lens frame, in
# opposite directions for the two windows, until both graphs walked
# off-screen. Focus the lens, which redraws continuously, and the nodes
# vanish from both.
#
# `assert visible` is the whole point: it fails the moment every node is
# off-screen, which is exactly what drift produces. Offline; FRESH profile.
settle 30
key escape

open mere://alpha
open mere://beta
wait
assert nodes >= 2
assert visible
capture 01_primary_before_lens

# Open a lens and let it render a long run of frames. Pre-fix, this is where
# the two cameras walked apart.
act New window
settle 60
assert windows == 2
assert visible
capture 02_primary_keeps_its_camera

# The lens draws the SAME graph through its own camera, not an empty canvas.
capture-lens 03_lens_draws_the_graph

# Still framed after another long run.
settle 40
assert visible
capture 04_primary_still_framed

log lens camera drift guard complete
